title('Engineering handoff / 18 October 2026','A finished frontend.<br/>A clear path to live work.')
p('Gigwork combines funded quick and agent tasks, milestone gigs, and ongoing contracts. Gigwork replaces the former Workloom brand. The original 16 October 2026 Overview (9 pages) and Backend (10 pages) are included unchanged under docs/source. This handoff separates implemented sample behavior from production requirements. Open the delivered website first, then connect the backend without redesigning it.')
table([['Status','What is evidenced'],['CURRENT','React + Vite website, nine product guides, worker/client workspace, local forms and state transitions, custom mascots, illustrated marketplace, dedicated job pages, responsive layouts and native chart controls.'],['REQUIRED','Authenticated ownership, policy and quality services, independent calibration, escrows, review assignment, reserves, receipts, keepers, retention and payouts.'],['PROPOSED','Service-adapter and persistence additions are proposals. Original contract interfaces, M1-M11 milestones and the source schema remain requirements; POST /v1/batches is explicitly specified.'],['UNRESOLVED','Verified chain/token addresses, provider availability, issuer terms, production fees, secrets, policy owners and font licensing. No real funds or accounts are connected.']],[84,427])
h('Preserve the approved design direction')
p('The marketing page retains Jasper\'s section sequence, serif typography, flat framing and geometric scenes, with Gigwork copy and generated mascots. The later dashboard correction uses the supplied Panze screenshot: a slim icon rail, soft modular grid, gridded progress bars and native charts in Gigwork colours. Do not replace it with a generic dashboard kit.')
h('Runtime and state')
p('<b>Source:</b> src/main.jsx, src/Dashboard.jsx, src/DashboardOverview.jsx, src/Marketplace.jsx, src/domain.js and their CSS. The sample store is gigwork-product-preview-v1 in localStorage. Role switching is a demonstration and provides no authentication or authorization. New browsers receive seed data; no personal workspace is bundled.')
p('<b>Open now:</b> extract the ZIP; on Windows run START-GIGWORK.cmd, or run node scripts/serve.mjs --open in the gigwork folder. Node is required; no package install, account or backend is needed for the included build. Use the address printed in the terminal.','WLSmall')
story.append(PageBreak())
title('01 / Replace local state deliberately','Service boundaries and ownership.')
table([['Frontend entry','Production replacement'],['Dashboard: readState / setData','Authenticated bootstrap and role-scoped queries. Cache validated server state; never trust browser balances or role flags.'],['taskAction / TaskModal / ReviewModal','Atomic claim lease, submit, release, approve or dispute. Server owns claim/review clocks and credited status.'],['BatchModal / batchQuote','Policy clearance, calibrated p65 estimate, signed reserve quote, exact-amount funding receipt before listing.'],['gigAction / TextModal','Owned milestone command endpoints; durable delivery references, progress timestamps, deadline and grace paths.'],['Contracts component','Reserved ledger, worker-approved future terms, paidThrough checkpoint and receipt-driven run/stream settlement.'],['WithdrawModal / StockModal / Profile','Destination verification, eligibility and risk acknowledgement, payout receipts, selected-history reveal and distinct-client count.']],[181,330])
h('Identity and persistence')
p('<b>Required:</b> passkey-backed account plus second device or backup signer; owner/worker/client roles attached to server identity; pseudonymous worker IDs per batch. Separate public address commitments from private task content. A device attestation does not prove a unique person.')
p('<b>Source schema:</b> Backend p. 8 supplies requesters, workers, batches, items, assignments, gigs, milestones, contracts, reviews and payouts. <b>Proposed additions:</b> accounts/sessions, claim leases, command-idempotency records, immutable ledger/reservation entries, funding receipts, outbox jobs, reports and history reveals. Use integer token units, record versions and indexed deadlines. Keep fees and reserves separate.')
h('Command contract')
p('<b>Proposed:</b> each mutation accepts an idempotency key and expected record version. Return the accepted record, server time, status and receipt/job identifiers. Map conflicts to a refreshed view, expired leases to release/reclaim, and provider outages to a retryable state. UI states: validating, awaiting signature, submitted, confirming, confirmed, failed and retryable. Never infer settled payment from a successful HTTP response alone.')
p('The brief proposes Bun/TypeScript, Hono + tRPC, Drizzle/Postgres (+ Timescale), BullMQ/Redis, viem and Foundry contracts. These are requirements to validate; this delivery installs none of that backend.','WLSmall')
story.append(PageBreak())
title('02 / Enforce beyond the UI','Funding and review invariants.')
h('Quick and agent tasks')
p('Fund before listing. Capture type, instructions, items, workers per item, test-question rate, pay, claim limit, review window, region and language. Minimum review: 24 hours. Independent eligible calibrators produce the p65 time estimate; estimated pay must meet $6/hour. Track realized rates; require a top-up within three days of a breach or cancel/refund only unclaimed work.')
p('Test questions are paid. Accuracy is per type: below 80% over the last 50 test questions pauses that type with appeal/retraining. Accuracy or agreement cannot cut listed pay. Ordinary refunds cannot touch submitted or disputed assignments. Reject with a reason; delayed reviewer draw; 72-hour review deadline, one escalation and the specified 144-hour hard cap. Implement all paths with exactly-once credit.')
h('Gigs and contracts')
p('List gigs only after milestone one is funded. Fund every later milestone before start. Review minimum: 72 hours. Normal cancellation applies only before start; overdue work follows deadline + 72-hour grace and reviewer allocation for recorded partial work. Preserve delivery notes and evidence, not just UI status.')
p('Reserve the next full contract period before it starts; insufficient reserve pauses work. Admins can withdraw only unreserved funds. A single paidThrough checkpoint coordinates scheduled and streamed pay. Worker consent changes the next period only. Ending pays the larger of notice-period pay or the current reserved period. Generate pay statements, not employment payslips.')
h('Amounts, payouts and worker rights')
p('Clients pay 12% on quick/agent tasks, 8% on gigs and 1% per Pay run capped at $15, plus separately quoted review reserves. Workers keep full listed pay. USDG is the default; stock allocation begins at 0%. The brief excludes US/UK/CA/CH; final issuer eligibility must be verified. Show issuer-product risks and route costs; stale, closed or failed routes fall back to USDG. Never suggest token picks or forecasts.')
p('WorkerPass Tier 0 has no stake and capped volume; Tiers 1/2 require $10/$50 USDG plus accuracy. Stake exits: 14 days, at most one named-review freeze, 30 days total. Tips apply only to credited work and at most 100% of item pay; tipper pays route costs. BonusVault is outside worker pay with a fixed capped budget. These staking, tip and reward services are not implemented.')
p('<b>Privacy:</b> task/gig content deletion 60 days after close, export beforehand; hashed device fingerprints 90 days. Selected history sharing reveals payout address/public payments, must show distinct clients and flag linked-account entries.','WLSmall')
story.append(PageBreak())
title('03 / Integration acceptance','Connect, verify, then release.')
p('These are cross-cutting integration gates, not a replacement for the original M1-M11 order on the next page. No live adapters, APIs or backend services are installed by this handoff.','WLSmall')
table([['Phase','Acceptance gate'],['1. Accounts + data','Authenticate both roles; enforce object ownership and schemas server-side. A second account cannot read private items or approve another client\'s work. Restore/recover a passkey account without a frontend bypass.'],['2. Funded task loop','Policy scan, independent quote and exact funding receipt precede listing. Claim race has one winner. Replay submit/approve 10 times and credit once. Expiry/default paths use server clocks; failed jobs recover safely.'],['3. Reviews + payouts','Delayed draw excludes linked accounts; reason/evidence retained; reserve shortage has a defined path; deadlines resolve deterministically. Failed payout remains retryable without duplicate transfer.'],['4. Gigs + contracts','No normal cancellation after start. Partial-work dispute and grace paths tested. Reserve cannot be withdrawn. Accepted future rate leaves current pay unchanged. Run + stream never double-pay.'],['5. History + optional routes','Privacy acknowledgement precedes live share; independent reveal verifies commitment. Country/issuer checks and oracle freshness precede stock route; every fallback returns USDG. Keep Local tasks gated.']],[117,394])
h('Jobs, monitoring and recovery')
p('<b>Proposed jobs:</b> claim expiry, default approvals, delayed draws, review deadlines, calibration breach timers, payout batches, contract reserve/run schedules, stake exits and retention deletion. Every worker uses bounded retries and idempotent keys; failures enter a dead-letter queue. Alert on stale funding receipts, overdue reviews, ledger mismatch, insufficient reserves, stale prices and payout age. Provide reconciliation and replay tools before launch.')
h('Deployment decisions still required')
p('The supplied chain ID, USDG/Permit2 behavior, RPC/bundler selection, sponsorship assumptions and stock-token issuer routes are not independently verified here. The backend owner must confirm exact addresses, decimals, deployment/network capabilities, issuer terms and provider limits against current official sources before enabling a transaction. Product/legal owners must approve eligibility, notices, terms, privacy and permitted work; no owner names or launch dates were supplied.')
p('Use separate preview/staging/production environments, server-held secrets, migrations with rollback, signed webhooks and release receipts. The current Site is owner-private; the ZIP does not transfer its access. Production services must replace sample state without changing the finished UI. Source briefs are included privately under docs/source; launch tactics were not copied into public claims.','WLSmall')
story.append(PageBreak())

title('04 / Original specification order','The backend build queue.')
p('Required sequence from Backend pp. 9-10. Planning durations are not delivery promises. Detailed requirements, source-page traceability and acceptance checks are in docs/BACKEND-IMPLEMENTATION.md.')
table([['Step','Scope and gate'],['M1','TaskEscrow + ReviewerSet. Fund-before-list, lease/review/default/draw/refund/topUp and fuzz invariants. Prove no submitted or disputed pay can be refunded.'],['M2','WorkerPass, device attestation, tiers, StakeVault. Recovery, stake exit/freeze/appeal bounds, screening and real object ownership.'],['M3','Policy, independent calibration, matching. Screen every entry point; independent p65 estimate and $6/hour floor; enforce language, region and tier.'],['M4','Quality, test questions, agreement, appeals, results API. Paid tests, per-type accuracy pause, retirement of contested tests and no pay reduction.'],['M5','Connect existing web frontend, USDG PayoutRouter and pay handles. Authenticated work-to-credit flow, receipts, withdrawals and offline defaults.'],['M6','Agent REST/SDK/MCP + x402; Test/Label. Atomic create+fund, batch-hash witness, same policy rules, safe synthetic-account testing.'],['M7','GigEscrow + client dashboard. Acceptance/start/progress, funded milestones, delivery, extensions, >=72h review and overdue partial-work split.'],['M8','PayRuns + statements. Reserved periods, run/stream sharing one paidThrough, next-period rate consent and notice settlement.'],['M9','Optional stock legs, holdings and tips. Verified eligibility, oracle/market checks, 0.5% bound, depth caps and per-worker USDG fallback.'],['M10','WorkHistory/reveal pages and separate BonusVault. Escrow-only commitments, chosen reveals, distinct clients and cluster flags. Telegram only if permitted.'],['M11','Local tasks. Validated capture, blur/EXIF removal, coarse geofence/time, repeat-target limits and public-commercial categories only.']],[54,457])
p('<b>Mandatory release evidence:</b> approveDefault, resolveDefault, refundUnclaimed, run, reserveNext, payoutBatch and withdraw with Gigwork services stopped. Fuzz double pay, reserved-fund drains, cancellation/refund boundaries and delayed-draw predictability against a simulated sequencer. External review before relevant caps exceed $5,000.','WLSmall')
story.append(PageBreak())

title('05 / Developer transfer','Open it. Keep it. Connect it.')
h('Start from the exact delivered frontend')
p('The ZIP contains editable React/Vite source, lockfile, built dist, all runtime artwork/fonts, original briefs, generators and visual evidence. Tested toolchain: Node 24.19.0 and pnpm 11.25.0; declared minimum Node 22.12.0. Node itself is not bundled. The preview requires no dependency installation. For development: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile; pnpm dev --port 5173. Validate with pnpm test and pnpm build.')
p('Windows: START-GIGWORK.cmd. macOS/Linux: sh START-GIGWORK.command. Cross-platform: node scripts/serve.mjs --open. The preview tries port 4173 and subsequent free ports, prints the URL and opens a browser. Keep its terminal running. Do not open dist/index.html as a file. The delivered launcher serves only dist, never the internal PDFs.')
h('Read the implementation maps')
table([['File','Use'],['CODEX-START-HERE.md / START-HERE.md','Open gigwork/ as the Codex project. Setup, first prompt, commands and troubleshooting.'],['docs/BACKEND-IMPLEMENTATION.md','Original-page traceability, exact M1-M11 scope, monetary/quality/privacy rules and unresolved configuration.'],['docs/FRONTEND-INTEGRATION.md','Route/handler map, local state seams, proposed adapter boundary and real failure states.'],['docs/DEPLOYMENT.md','Environment separation, hosting fallback, secret/configuration inventory and release/recovery gates.'],['docs/SOURCE-AUDIT.md / QA.md','All 19 original pages accounted for, known gaps and unresolved decisions; evidence preserves the approved design.']],[197,314])
h('Make the boundary explicit')
p('No live backend, wallet, database, signer, contracts, provider credentials or reviewer service is included. The role switch and localStorage store are samples. New browsers start with seed data; personal browser state is not transferred. Optional regeneration tools do not have to be installed to run the website.')
p('The portable ZIP omits the owner-only Site binding and Git/plugin metadata. Private hosted access is separate from this source transfer. No access policy was changed. Deploy only dist with SPA fallback; keep internal documents private. Confirm font licensing and every unverified chain/provider/issuer assumption before its dependent production milestone.')
p('<b>First live slice:</b> keep the appearance unchanged; connect one screened and funded Judge/Verify batch through authenticated discovery, claim, submission, review and receipt-confirmed credit. Test competing claims, wrong-account access, expiry, signature cancellation, outage/retry, replayed credit and service-offline default approval. Existing six sample tests are not contract fuzzing or a security audit.','WLSmall')
